# Line endings.
#
# ⚠️ THE RULE THAT MATTERS: anything that is executed or parsed INSIDE a Linux
# container must be checked out with LF endings, on every platform.
#
# This repository is developed on Windows, where `core.autocrlf=true` is the
# default and Git rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout. That is harmless for C# — and
# fatal for a shell script bind-mounted into a container: `/bin/sh` reads the
# carriage return as part of the last word on every line, so `set -eu` becomes
# `set -eu\r` and the script dies with errors that name characters you cannot
# see. The stack would boot on the machine that authored it and fail on the next
# Windows clone, which is the worst possible failure to debug.
#
# Added with M0-03 (the local dev stack) for exactly that reason. Extend it
# whenever a new file starts being read by a container rather than by the .NET
# build.

# Let Git decide what is text, and normalise it to LF in the repository.
* text=auto

# ---------------------------------------------------------- container inputs
# Executed or parsed inside a Linux container: LF, always, everywhere.
*.sh              text eol=lf
infra/**          text eol=lf
docker-compose.yml     text eol=lf
docker-compose.*.yml   text eol=lf
.env.example      text eol=lf
.dockerignore     text eol=lf
**/Dockerfile     text eol=lf
Dockerfile        text eol=lf

# CI scripts run on ubuntu runners under pwsh, which copes with either, but LF
# keeps the diffs clean.
build/ci/*.ps1    text eol=lf
build/git/*.ps1   text eol=lf

# Git hooks are read by /bin/sh — the same rule as the container inputs above,
# and the same failure if it is forgotten: `#!/bin/sh\r` is not an interpreter
# any Unix has. They have no .sh suffix because git chooses their names.
build/git/hooks/* text eol=lf

# ------------------------------------------------------------------- binary
*.png             binary
*.jpg             binary
*.jpeg            binary
*.webp            binary
*.ico             binary
*.ogg             binary
*.wav             binary
*.mp3             binary
*.ttf             binary
*.otf             binary
*.zip             binary
*.pck             binary
*.aab             binary
*.apk             binary
